87914ac9-c111-44d6-a367-eb679a93374f	dc099dcb-289c-476b-99ed-d29d486b7c7b	0cd6f10d-fa83-4df4-a3b4-5d9d202aace5	\N	Recall Check: Why Agents Learn	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"text": "The three reasons from page 1 are: (1) designers cannot anticipate all possible situations (like a robot navigating a new maze), (2) designers cannot anticipate changes over time (like a stock market shifting from boom to bust), and (3) sometimes human programmers have no idea how to program a solution themselves (like recognizing family faces).", "type": "paragraph"}], "version": 1}	{"kind": "self", "label": "Pages 1–3"}	[{"page": 1, "knowledge_item_id": "136cd389-8be9-4f12-937f-8bcbc5acf96a"}]	1	2026-09-01 22:40:23.8474+03	2026-09-01 22:40:23.8474+03
9f8020aa-c82f-41bd-a410-6c4776c11a2b	dc099dcb-289c-476b-99ed-d29d486b7c7b	0cd6f10d-fa83-4df4-a3b4-5d9d202aace5	\N	Tunnelling & Ladder Safety Basics	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"text": "When working in construction and tunnelling contexts, safety procedures such as proper ladder use are essential to prevent slips, falls, and injuries. According to the course materials, improper ladder use accounts for 20% of fatal and lost workday injuries in general industry, making equipment inspection and correct setup critical first steps. Safe tunnelling and general construction practices rely on careful preparation, rigorous equipment inspection, and adherence to established setup guidelines to prevent workplace falls.", "type": "paragraph"}], "version": 1}	{"kind": "self", "label": "TUNNELLING"}	[{"page": 51, "knowledge_item_id": "3d013096-89b2-42cb-b638-88e6f3c75362"}]	1	2026-09-02 11:18:31.774289+03	2026-09-02 11:18:31.774289+03
ff35392d-558f-4d6a-9524-cad33ea5bebd	dc099dcb-289c-476b-99ed-d29d486b7c7b	0cd6f10d-fa83-4df4-a3b4-5d9d202aace5	\N	Deeper Look: Why Agents Learn from Examples	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"text": "At a core level, agent learning is about adaptability. Instead of hardcoding every possible rule, designers build systems that observe their environment and update their internal logic to handle new tasks. Pages 1–3 of your material focus on why this capability is necessary rather than optional. Agents learn from examples because real-world environments are too unpredictable, dynamic, and complex for humans to manually write rules for every scenario.", "type": "paragraph"}], "version": 1}	{"kind": "self", "label": "Pages 1–3"}	[{"page": 1, "knowledge_item_id": "136cd389-8be9-4f12-937f-8bcbc5acf96a"}]	1	2026-09-02 11:32:17.141432+03	2026-09-02 11:32:17.141432+03
734b267b-c510-45fc-9946-7a0311b672b0	dc099dcb-289c-476b-99ed-d29d486b7c7b	0cd6f10d-fa83-4df4-a3b4-5d9d202aace5	\N	Tunnelling & Ladder Safety Concept Map	{"type": "doc", "content": [{"text": "Ladder safety involves planning setup height and material, inspecting for defects and slip hazards, and following safe operating rules such as locking A-frame arms.", "type": "paragraph"}], "version": 1}	{"kind": "self", "label": "TUNNELLING"}	[{"page": 51, "knowledge_item_id": "3d013096-89b2-42cb-b638-88e6f3c75362"}]	1	2026-09-02 12:24:20.87474+03	2026-09-02 12:24:20.87474+03
