he same point.", "routeChange": "Paused at “Tunnelling & Ladder Safety Concept Map” to answer your question.", "observationId": "491f69a9-46a4-46d0-b5a9-a4cd6954b878", "acknowledgement": "The supplied construction safety and tunnelling material does not contain information defining cement, so I cannot verify a course-specific definition for it. Now, returning to our lesson on tunnelling and ladder safety, let's look at how proper equipment selection and inspection keep workers safe from falls.", "changedDecisionId": null}, {"id": "59314fd2-84ac-4f34-a63a-bbba087d065e", "action": "answer_now", "status": "rejoined", "question": "Can you define cement in general?", "createdAt": "2026-09-02T09:18:14.783Z", "rejoinedAt": "2026-09-02T09:18:34.350Z", "returnPlan": "After you confirm the answer makes sense, return to “Tunnelling & Ladder Safety Concept Map” at the same point.", "routeChange": "Paused at “Tunnelling & Ladder Safety Concept Map” to answer your question.", "observationId": "20bc38d7-5531-4528-95da-2c02a2ce0dcc", "acknowledgement": "Cement is a binder, a substance used in construction that sets, hardens, and adheres to other materials to bind them together. While it is not mentioned in our current lesson on ladder safety, cement is commonly mixed with water, sand, and gravel to make concrete. For example, Portland cement is the most common type of cement used worldwide as a key ingredient in mortar and concrete.", "changedDecisionId": null}], "version": 5, "maxMoves": 5, "createdAt": "2026-09-02T08:16:45.398Z", "updatedAt": "2026-09-02T09:18:16.441Z", "checkpoints": [{"id": "checkpoint-1", "label": "Find the useful entry", "status": "complete"}, {"id": "checkpoint-2", "label": "Build the idea", "status": "current"}, {"id": "checkpoint-3", "label": "Bring it back", "status": "pending"}, {"id": "checkpoint-4", "label": "Make it yours", "status": "pending"}, {"id": "checkpoint-5", "label": "Close it out", "status": "pending"}], "closeReason": null, "currentGoal": 