 check it with one explanation or example.", "sessionType": "learn", "stateVersion": "petros.session-state.v3", "topicProfile": {"cacheKey": "73ed97715f7b74166a13b9767f1005630a6c08f5f7131bffba94014d5f3eb3c1", "profileId": "cfd4fce6-bd83-4f91-8692-c47ed5899b99", "resolution": "canonical", "knowledgeTypes": ["conceptual"], "overrideVersion": null, "representations": ["verbal", "comparative"], "canonicalVersion": 1, "canonicalVersionId": "ae6b4a8d-702f-4fab-8cf3-d2044540763b"}, "sourceContext": {"door": "uploaded_document", "label": "Construction Safety, Tunnelling & Ergonomics — Module 3 · selected pages", "intentId": "9090a8b2-03ce-4398-ac98-50c40765c15b", "citations": [{"page": 51, "label": "Construction Safety, Tunnelling & Ergonomics — Module 3 (p. 51–60)", "excerpt": "Slide 51 Ladder safety Ladders can pose serious potential for a fall if used improperly or in an unsafe manner. OSHA estimates that, for general industry companies, falls from ladders account for 20% of fatal and lost workday injuries. This Photo by Unknown Author is licensed under CC BY-SA-NC Slide 52 Ladder setup First, choose the right ladder. Questions to ask What height will I have to reach and work at? What should I check before using the ladder? What type of material should it be made of? These Photos by Unknown Author are licensed under CC BY-SA Slide 53 Ladder setup Ladder inspection Ladder label Skid resistant footing Free of defects Free of slipping hazards This Photo by Unknown Author is licensed under CC BY-SA This Photo by Unknown Author is licensed under CC BY-SA-NC Slide 54 Safe use of ladders Ensuring the ladder is secure Folding ladders Folding or A-frame ladders should be fully extended and the arms locked into place. Be careful of pinch points which are any places where parts come together and present a possibility for injury. Never use a step ladder as an extension ladder This Photo by Unknown Author is licensed under CC BY-SA Slide 55 Safe use of ladders Ensur", "section": "TUNNELLING", "version": "1:76ab940581b91568", "sourceId": "3d013096-89b2-42cb-b638-88e6f3c75362", "sourceType": "document"}], "pageIndex": 50, "returnHref": "/materials", "referenceId": "3d013096-89b2-42cb-b638-88e6f3c75362", "resumeToken": "d0ccd2fc-e054-48ce-8fca-a0c8917c0b3d", "returnLabel": "Study materials", "registerFactors": ["The student explicitly asked to be taught from their own uploaded pages.", "Keep source grounding visible and separate explanation from quotation."], "emotionalRegister": "curious_grounded", "policyDisclosures": ["Petros uses only extracted pages available to this student and cites their page numbers.", "Document teaching is for explanation and limited quotation; the original file remains the source."], "sourceFingerprint": "8e59b693504a938cff44140a5313b9e67df75df9f90a1a133326871433e99223", "institutionalDecision": {"homework": null, "syllabus": {"decision": "within_bounds", "allowedDepth": 3, "teachingShape": "normal", "requestedTopic": "TUNNELLING", "sourceBoundary": {"approvedSourceIds": [], "externalSourcesAllowed": false}, "studentMessage": "This topic is inside your institution's approved learning scope."}}}, "elapsedSeconds": 292, "fallbackNotice": null, "personalization": {"status": "neutral", "reasons": ["deep depth and deliberate pace are supported by 25 observed actions.", "Confidence is still fragile across 10 checked answers, so an earlier recheck is useful."], "sessionOverride": null}, "expectedMoveType": null, "timeBudgetSeconds": 900, "observationSummary": {"correct": 0, "partial": 0, "answered": 0, "incorrect": 0, "openDetours": 3, "fragileSuccesses": 0, "activeStruggleLevel": 0, "activeWrongAttemptCount": 0, "highValueMisconceptions": 0}, "currentCheckpointId": "checkpoint-2", "institutionalPolicy": {"disclosure": {"homeworkRule": "While related homework is active, Petros will use questions, hints, setup and feedback instead of giving the final answer.", "syllabusRule": "Petros stays within approved syllabus sources only,